https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eDAaKxlaBQ4  (Capo 0)

TIP:  Of course this is a Bob Dylan tune, and it's great poetry, but Bob was all over the map with his version and I much prefer George's version.  Neither recording charted, in fact the only version that did was the Olivia Newton-John cover in 1971 but her's is a bit on the syrupy side.

TIP:  The (G) - (D) - (C) drives the whole verse and it comes right on the heels of the last word in the line so it's important to get the rhythm down.

TIP:  There's a little step-down at the end of the bridge.  End with a single strum of |D7| and begin the next verse without a chord until (G) "you".


